      },
      {
        "label": "Caption",
        "value": "If one had to describe an elevator in three words: leaky, shaking and untrustworthy wouldn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t be the first thing most students think of \u00e2\u0080\u0093 unless you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re talking about the Kent State library. \n\nOver five decades old, the Kent State library elevators are the original models from 1970, and it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s easy to tell. Unlit buttons, rough shaking, oil leaking from the lights, to even going to the wrong floor, the three library elevators are overdue for a remodel. \n\nStudents aren\u00e2\u0080\u0099t the only ones who seem to think so, as $10 million has been allocated to go towards an elevator modernization project, after the Board of Trustees of Kent State University approved the remodel in a September 2024 meeting. There\u00e2\u0080\u0099s just one caveat: patience. \n\n\u00f0\u009f\u0093\u00b0Aryn Kauble\n\u00f0\u009f\u0093\u00b7Aryn Kauble"
      },
      {
        "label": "Title",
